<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gusti Ketut Jelantik</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1849">1849</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gusti Ketut Jelantik was the patih (chief minister) of the Balinese kingdom of Buleleng and the leader of its resistance to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a>. He refused Dutch demands over the plundering of shipwrecks and in 1848 defeated a Dutch expedition at the fortress of Jagaraga. A larger Dutch force took Jagaraga in 1849, and he was killed soon after. He is a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/national-hero-of-indonesia">National Hero of Indonesia</a>.</p></div>
